  "reference_notes": "Compared the three actual photographs with revised three-size pilots and all 36 variants. Corrected the generic twice-divided fern to single lanceolate pinnae, increased the number of pinna pairs and upright fronds, and narrowed the frond envelope. This preserves the dense erect-to-arching western sword fern tuft and distinguishes it from male and lady ferns. Current heights span 0.47-1.09 m. Fine pinna teeth, basal auricles and sori are unresolved at 25 mm. Accepted as stylized spring sword fern, pending user endorsement.",
